# Chat Artifacts Subsystem — Full architecture

Renderable reports (md/html/svg) become first-class rows in
`chat_artifacts` so they survive compaction, can be re-opened in a
right-side panel by stable URL, and can be versioned, pinned, and
exported as PDF independently of the conversation.  Producers detect
artifacts deterministically — the LLM is NOT taught about them, same
philosophy as the `paper-report-image-injection` memory.

## Schema (chat_artifacts; version 18)
- Table is `chat_artifacts` — NOT `artifacts` (that name is taken by
  the in-memory swarm artifact store; PK mapping registered in
  `lib/database/_sql_translate.py`).
- Columns: id (PK), conv_id, task_id, msg_id, source, source_ref (JSON),
  format, title, content, content_sha256, size_bytes, version, parent_id,
  pinned (BOOLEAN on PG, INTEGER on SQLite — pass Python `bool` to
  `db_execute_with_retry`, NOT 0/1 ints, otherwise PG raises
  DatatypeMismatch), meta (JSON), created_at, deleted_at (soft delete).
- Indexes: (conv_id, created_at DESC), (conv_id, msg_id),
  (conv_id, content_sha256), (task_id).

## lib/artifacts package
- `core.py` — `create_artifact`, `get_artifact`, `get_artifact_meta`,
  `list_artifacts`, `delete_artifact` (soft), `set_pinned`,
  `list_versions`, `list_pinned_or_recent`, predicates
  `is_renderable_path` / `detect_format`.  Hard cap 8 MiB.  Per-conv
  dedupe via `content_sha256`.  **Versioning**: same `(conv_id,
  source_ref.path)` with NEW content auto-stamps `version=N+1` and
  `parent_id` to the previous live row.  Same content still dedupes.
- `events.py` — `emit_artifact_event(task, meta)` appends an `artifact`
  SSE event via `lib.tasks_pkg.manager.append_event`.  **Content is
  NEVER in the event** — only metadata + `/api/artifacts/<id>/raw`.
- `scanner.py` — Producer B: `scan_message(conv_id, text, msg_id, task_id, task)`.
  Detects ```html / ```markdown / ```md / ```svg above thresholds
  (`_MIN_FENCE_BYTES=2048` OR `_MIN_FENCE_LINES=80`) AND bare
  `<!doctype html>` / `<html>` regions including streamed truncations.
  Mask-then-scan: fenced spans are blanked before bare-HTML regex runs,
  so a fenced HTML block is NOT also detected as `inline_doc`.
- `pdf_export.py` — `render_artifact_pdf(id) -> bytes`.  Markdown via
  `markdown_it` (commonmark, `html=False` so model HTML in markdown
  source is escaped, not passed through).  HTML wrapped in a print CSS
  template; full-document HTML is passed through after `<script>`
  stripping.  All rendering goes through the shared
  `lib.fetch.playwright_pool` worker via a new `pdf_render` task kind
  with `java_script_enabled=False` and `page.route('**/*', abort)`.

## Producers
- **A — write_file hook**: `lib/tasks_pkg/handlers/project.py:_maybe_promote_write_to_artifact`.
  Runs after successful `write_file` / `apply_diff` / `insert_content`.
  Reads canonical bytes from disk, persists, emits SSE.  Per-feature
  cap `_WRITE_ARTIFACT_MAX_BYTES = 1 MiB`.  Stamps `meta.artifactId`
  on the tool round meta.  Best-effort — failures don't break the round.
  **Markdown is intentionally NOT promoted** by Producer A: routine
  project doc edits (README.md, CHANGELOG.md, etc.) shouldn't spawn
  chips.  Only `.html` / `.htm` / `.svg` reach `create_artifact` from
  this path.  Inline ```markdown fences still go through Producer B
  (scanner.py).
- **B — inline scanner**: wired in
  `lib/tasks_pkg/orchestrator.py:_finalize_and_emit_done` immediately
  before `persist_task_result(task)`.  Both producers gated by
  `lib.ARTIFACTS_ENABLED` (env `ARTIFACTS_ENABLED=0` or
  `data/config/features.json:artifacts_enabled` to disable).

## Routes — `routes/artifacts.py` (blueprint `artifacts_bp`, registered last)
- `GET    /api/artifacts/<id>` — metadata only.
- `GET    /api/artifacts/<id>/raw` — raw bytes with strict CSP (see
  Security Invariants below).
- `GET    /api/artifacts/<id>/versions` — version chain (oldest→newest).
- `GET    /api/artifacts/<id>/export?format=pdf` — Playwright PDF render.
- `GET    /api/artifacts/conv/<conv_id>` — list metadata for a conv.
- `GET    /api/artifacts/library?limit=50` — pinned first, then recent
  (cross-conversation).
- `POST   /api/artifacts/<id>/pin` — `{pinned: bool}`.
- `DELETE /api/artifacts/<id>` — soft-delete.
- `POST   /api/artifacts/scan/<conv_id>` — backfill: re-scan an
  existing conversation's assistant messages (idempotent via dedupe).

## Frontend — `static/js/artifacts.js`
- `window.Artifacts` API: `open(id)`, `closePanel()`,
  `attachToMessage(msg, meta)`, `renderChips(arr)`,
  `hydrateConversation(conv)`.
- Right-side panel, resizable (drag handle on left edge, persisted to
  `localStorage[tofu.artifactPanel.width]`), full-screen on mobile.
- Tabs: **Doc** (current artifact) + **Library** (cross-conv list).
- Header: format badge, version `<select>` (only shown when chain >1),
  copy/download/PDF/print/pin/close buttons.
- **Markdown** rendered via `renderMarkdown` (DOMPurify-cleaned).
- **HTML** rendered in `<iframe sandbox="" srcdoc=...>`.  Banner offers
  "Allow scripts (this session)"; consent drops `allow-same-origin`
  and uses `sandbox="allow-scripts"` ALONE — the only spec-safe combo
  with scripts.  Consent is per-session, NOT persisted; logged via
  `/api/client-error` for audit.
- **SVG** rendered as data: URI when scriptless, else iframe path.
- Keyboard: `Esc` closes panel; `Ctrl/Cmd+P` prints (iframe.print()
  for HTML/SVG, falls back to PDF download for markdown).
- SSE handler in `static/js/ui.js` for `ev.type === "artifact"` stashes
  meta on `assistantMsg._artifacts` and triggers `twUpdate(convId)`.
  Chip rendered just below file-changes bar.
- Hydration in `static/js/core.js:loadConversationMessages` (cache-load
  AND server-load paths) calls `Artifacts.hydrateConversation` →
  `GET /api/artifacts/conv/<conv_id>` → attaches by `_msgId` (with
  last-assistant fallback for legacy rows).

## CRITICAL: bundler trap (CLAUDE.md §3.2.1)
`artifacts.js` is in `lib/js_bundler.py:_BUNDLE_FILES` between
`branch.js` and `ui.js`.  `tests/test_artifacts_bundle_registration.py`
enforces this AND every static/js/*.js referenced in index.html being
present (compaction-viewer.js intentionally excluded).  When adding
NEW top-level JS, follow the same pattern or it loads as a silent
no-op in production.

## Playwright pool dispatch (lib/fetch/playwright_pool.py)
The pool's worker loop uses task-kind discrimination:
  * Legacy fetches: `((url, timeout, max_chars), result_q)` — 3-tuple.
  * `pdf_render`: `(('pdf_render', {'html', 'title'}), result_q)`.
Discrimination rule: `isinstance(payload, tuple) and len(payload)==2
and isinstance(payload[0], str)`.  `tests/test_playwright_pool_dispatch.py`
guards this.

## SECURITY INVARIANTS — DO NOT RELAX
- `/api/artifacts/<id>/raw` returns `Content-Security-Policy: sandbox;
   default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline' https:; img-src data:
   https:; font-src ...; media-src ...`.  No `allow-scripts`.  Even a
  top-level navigation cannot run model JS.
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`.
- Frontend must NEVER `innerHTML = modelHtml`.  HTML always renders
  in `<iframe sandbox srcdoc>`.
- The PDF render path runs in our shared playwright pool, so model
  HTML is `<script>`-stripped server-side and Chromium starts the
  context with `java_script_enabled=False` AND blocks all network
  via `page.route('**/*', abort)`.  Defense in depth.

