## Pitfalls / lessons learned
- Test fence size: keep ≥ 2× the threshold (`_make_long_html(repeats=8)`
  builds ~4 KB above the 2 KB cap).  4× margin is safer.
- Pinned column type: BOOLEAN on PG, INTEGER on SQLite — pass `bool`
  to `db_execute_with_retry` always.
- Backfill test fixtures must use unique conv_ids — pytest fixture DB
  is session-scoped, identical conv_ids leak rows across reruns.
- The session-scoped DB in tests is SHARED with the test PG/SQLite,
  so any cleanup matters for repeat runs.
- `compaction-viewer.js` is intentionally excluded from `_BUNDLE_FILES`.

